              {
                "detail": "Runtime instructions are focused and consistent with the stated purpose: use scripts/run.py commands, bootstrap the runtime, configure a SherpaDesk API token via `configure --api-key`, seed the local DB, and optionally install a user-level systemd service. The instructions reference only skill-local paths ('.SherpaMind/') and the SherpaDesk API host. They do not direct the agent to read unrelated system files or exfiltrate data to unknown endpoints. However, they do instruct creation of local runtime state and a persistent service which affects system behavior.",
                "label": "Instruction Scope",
